                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okay, so, tad annoyed I have to replay the game to get the Moobius achievement, for some reason it didn't trigger, but I actually liked this quite a bit otherwise. The animations are a bit janky (they show teeth a LOT when talking) and the 2D and 3D don't mix well sometimes and can be extremely noticeable (e.g. the medic in the ending is very obviously stood in front of a PNG. A poorly angled PNG that removes all illusion of depth too), but the writing was pretty solid, the voice work for most characters was great (a few characters with limited screen time weren't as good), and I got a few laughs out of parts of it (like the analysis of \"Cold, stern eyes = Missed a rerun of Friends\").\r\n\r\nAnd I know he's not everyone's cup of tea, but the protagonist really hit the \"arrogant douche genius\" archtype with the right amount of progression to his character and his more deranged acts later when forced to become more proactive really showed how much he'd changed. It felt like they actually wanted a movie or TV show plot, then made it work for the game. Plus I am quite happy there was a \"double click to teleport\" function, really helped speed things up even if interactions sometimes lagged.\r\n\r\nAlso, and I can't word this any other way so I have to put spoilers, [spoiler] intentional or not, I did like the ambiguity of the protagonist's relationship with the deuteragonist. The way you can read it as a bond of trust or even attraction made for an interesting development. Personally I read it in the latter, it somewhat enhanced the previously mentioned deranged acts and made it a matter of \"a man not wanting to admit he cares for another man, despite the fact he's resorting to violence for answers\".[/spoiler]\r\n\r\nCould've done with a little polish, but otherwise this has been great!",
